      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Conclusion**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-323",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This architecture represents a shift from “do-everything” agents to a modular, maintainable, and traceable system of cooperating components. By treating agents as strictly-scoped functions, containing memory, and leaning into explicit contracts, this design lays the foundation for a scalable and resilient multi-agent AI runtime."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-324",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "If desired, the next step could involve drafting concrete TypeScript implementations for the Orchestrator schema, ResearchAgent, and WeatherAgent—alongside a mockable test harness. Let me know if you’d like to proceed."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
